<title>ITALY: Italy's Trieste sees April CPI at -0.6 pct mo/mo.</title>
<headline>Italy's Trieste sees April CPI at -0.6 pct mo/mo.</headline>
<dateline>TRIESTE, Italy 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian city of Trieste said its April consumer price index stood at minus 0.6 percent month-on-month and 1.2 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>In March, Trieste's inflation rate was 0.1 percent and 2.2 percent respectively.</p>
<p>Trieste is one of 11 Italian cities publishing inflation data on Monday and Tuesday. The city's CPI has a weighting of 2.49 percent on the national index. The 11 sample cities have a combined weighting of 75.66 percent on the total index.  </p>
<p>Following is the breakdown of the price changes.</p>
<p>(figures in brackets refer to March 1997):</p>
<p>					    Month/Month     Year/Year</p>
<p>    General index		    -0.6   (0.1)     1.2  (2.2)</p>
<p>    Food				 -0.4   (0.2)     1.1  (2.2)</p>
<p>    Clothing and footwear	   0.6   (0.3)     2.8  (3.2)</p>
<p>    Housing and utility charges   0.2  (-0.2)     3.2  (4.9)</p>
<p>    Furniture			   0.0   (0.1)     2.8  (2.8)</p>
<p>    Health services		   0.0   (0.0)     1.9  (1.9)</p>
<p>    Transportation		   -4.8   (0.3)    -2.3  (3.1)</p>
<p>    Entertainment and culture     0.0  (-0.4)    -0.7 (-0.6)</p>
<p>    Education			   0.0   (0.0)     4.8  (5.1)</p>
<p>    Hotels and restaurants	  0.0   (0.7)     3.0  (3.8)</p>
<p>    Other goods or services	 0.1   (0.2)    -0.7 (-0.8)</p>
<p>	  -- Milan newsroom +392 66129526</p>
